{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way","id":441130,"title":"Pure 2120 Trinity: the CHILL way","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-14T02:56:09-07:00","id":441130,"title":"Pure 2120 Trinity: the CHILL way","content":"I'm interested in the way a particular poster here (EON's CHILL) has run the setting. I threatened to call CHILL to account and he took my challenge, but it really deserves its own topic rather than muddy other waters. If any of this is out of context i apologize, refer to page three of '<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials\">Post-publishing and fan-made materials'</a> for anything i've cut out here...<br /> <br /> I hate that i'm quoting myself, but here goes...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The pure original Aeon setting is something i hold in esteem and you're kind of the only representative of it that i've personally encountered who wasn't corrupted by the need to make it fit in with anything else. I may end up calling you to account on some of it one day, because i am sincerely curious how some elements of the story (quantakinesis, order purges, Doyen, Nippon, the Chromatic 'deceivers', Coalition Furies, etc...) figure into the setting as you see it. You've mentioned not accepting official sources too (eden &amp; maybe process 418 as printed), so knowing where you drew the line might make things a bit clearer.<br /> -points and nods forebodingly at CHILL-<br /> <br /> So how did you 'CHILL-rate' it? [ ] huh [ ] cool [ ] yeah not my thing<br /> -tease- </div> </div> </div>Which lead to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439925#post439925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I laugh at your foreboding nod, pfah!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it looks like it's on!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439925#post439925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahem.<br /> <br /> QuantaK. Relegated to history. All chibs dead or otherwise out of play. Gone. Boom. Stabby-stabby &amp; turned into sticky-paste. Not a PC option<br /> Order purges. There was really only 1 purge, see above - although the Docs were coming close and I had plans to split that order up following the DR series. Never actually got around to it though<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But they (QKs) were still essentially built for anti-aberrant duties, and purged for their experiments into the nature of taint? How were the Upeo not subject to a 'purge-like' attack? Why did they all leave during Esperanza, then? Was Eden not blown up back then or something?<br /> I was reading that Aesculapian purge too, it was Doyen over-reaction 101. Then, nothing about it in the Alien Encounter series. I expect it would have been a filler adventure between the end of AE: Deception and the Coalition ark arriving, but we may never know what the original intent there was there.<br /> How would you have split them, out of curiousity?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439925#post439925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doyen. Yep, used them as per the DR series of books. Made no real modifications to them and didn't use them again outside running those scenarios<br /> Nippon. Never used it. *shrug*. Didn't come up in game either. Skim-read the fluff once, but never had to come back to it.<br /> Chromatics. See Doyen answer above<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why did you think the Doyen were doing what they do? If the aberrants are all gone, why do the Doyen give a damn about some dimensionally locked terrestrial creatures?<br /> Nippon just makes really advanced hard-tech that no-one else can produce and sifted their land-mass prior to rebuilding themselves into a giant arcology over sixty years ago? Ok. I can see how that doesn't come up unless you rub the characters faces in it, but you never had head-canon to sort that strangeness out?<br /> Chromies would have been just fine in their home setting i imagine, but what about the 'Deceivers'? The 'human-like' aliens who were like gods and attracted the Doyen? More space-mad (i like that term), but very pretty abbies?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439925#post439925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Coalition. As per the Alien: Deception book, not used them since then<br /> 418. Didn't advance the timeline to it. If I had needed to, I'd have to come up with something else. Not sure what that would be, but it absolutely would not be introducing non-prometheus chamber psions / powers<br /> Eden. Blew up. All dead. Especially that annoying Nova that vanished the Chromatics at Karoo. Put the vanishing Chromatics down to some space-mad Abbie whose reasons remain a mystery *spooky music*<br /> While I'm at it - Teleporters. They did return, but I had them do so in minimal numbers and as NPC's, none of which I used in games outside of the DR series. Am apprehensive about the Porter's being returned and ready to play in the TC reboot. Prefer these to be back-story and not playable<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have my hands on Deception, but i thought there was an encounter with tainted Furies at the end there. -shrug- Might be my own head-canon growing wild, time for some pruning... I guess another hand-waved space-mad abbie would be fine for that element too, that's basically what i remember happened anyway - unless Rushing Mountain from Asia Ascendant was involved somehow.<br /> -shrug-<br /> The fact that you might've still used 418/Venezuela, is that because you still use it as a temporal clairsentient barrier?<br /> <br /> -standing ovation-<br /> Good riddance Apollo Milliken! I have a tough time with Apollo too - even in my world view, i would have done that a bit differently - but it does bring stuff together (Upeo purge &amp; the Chromie Fleet). I was kind of putting my eggs in the 'mind of a child' basket with him, an idiot wild-card who wants to be a comic book hero. Major Kid Miracleman/Superboy Prime vibes there. But just blowing him up would have made the next couple of years a bit less confronting for the Orders/Doyen. Your players never found the destruction of the Chromatic fleet warranted a less hand-wavey solution?<br /> <br /> I never really liked the teleporters as PCs, kind of like having a 2008 Nova in amongst the psion party with stronger versions of Warp, Teleport and teleport mastery (if memory serves). As non-Upeo PCs that would have sucked - everyone would've wanted to play Upeo/Starcrossed. But they <i>are</i> required for all but one extra-solar colonies (the bastards stopped all the generational arks, my poor, precious hard-science) and i wasn't letting go of that part of the setting for any reason - so the Upeo must remain. -sigh-<br /> Rebalancing the Teleportation modes may do a lot to address that, but teleporters prevent the setting from embracing light speed and relativistic travel, which is kind of sad - but baked in at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Personally incapable of posting without later editing. 03-14-2015, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T15:50:35-07:00","id":441900,"title":"","content":"OK, I just had a fairly long post ready to go and screwed up posting and lost the darned thing. Agghh. I'll take an other pass tomorrow. I hate my laptop right now.... *sigh*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T00:03:34-07:00","id":442247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=441900#post441900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, I just had a fairly long post ready to go and screwed up posting and lost the darned thing. Agghh. I'll take an other pass tomorrow. I hate my laptop right now.... *sigh*</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, lost data? Sheeee-it. Thanks for the effort none-the-less. I won't lose patience if it takes you a bit longer, my 'call to account' isn't so easily deflected.<br /> -tips hat-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T08:13:38-07:00","id":442556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way#post441130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, lost data? Sheeee-it. Thanks for the effort none-the-less. I won't lose patience if it takes you a bit longer, my 'call to account' isn't so easily deflected.<br /> -tips hat-</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it was entirely user error though. I really dislike the latest version of Windows and spend as little time on it as possible. I knew I should've done this on the Mac. OK. Here goes<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way#post441130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they (QKs) were still essentially built for anti-aberrant duties, and purged for their experiments into the nature of taint? </div> </div> </div> </div>To my mind the Chibs abilities were a check against the Aberrants that survived the war and went out to the stars - not Novas (who in my view all joined Divis Mal in his pocket universe). In my view, aside from a couple major players like Divis Mal and some Novas who went with him, most Aberrants left at the end of the Aberrant war were already pretty much driven crazy by their taint. Its these guys that head off to the stars where they mutate even further - much closer to 2120 era Aberrants as presented in the Aeon core book. These are what the Doyen, Qin and Coalition encounter. They're barely recognizable as Nova's (a term that didn't start getting used until the Aberrant RPG was published, much later).<br /> <br /> The Chibs were purged for a whole bunch of reasons, the one trotted out the most was 'in league with Aberrants'. As always with the Aeon setting, there's a bunch more going on. The Chibs experimenting far outside the boundaries the Doyen had hoped, S. K. Bhurano's refusal to back down when it all came to a head, personality conflicts between the Proxies, the Order's being terrified of humanity perceiving psions as just another type of Aberrant that should be collectively destroyed (a fear that comes up again later in the Huang-Marr incident). I'd put good money on Aeon screwing things up a couple times along the way too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way#post441130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How were the Upeo not subject to a 'purge-like' attack? Why did they all leave during Esperanza, then? Was Eden not blown up back then or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this wasn't a purge. There was an attempt to control, not wipe-out. It may be splitting hairs, but there's an important distinction. One of the big problems here is that Alex Cassel and Bolade Atwan really didn't get along. She point blank didn't trust the guy (probably with good reason, on reflection). Miscommunication, poor planning on behalf of the Proxies, a bit of not necessarily unwarranted paranoia from Atwan and yeah, power-keg ready to happen. They all fled because Atwan made it quite clear that remaining meant being stripped of your teleportation powers. Not much of a choice, really. Those left behind were not porters anymore, with the exception of some on the far colonies. <br /> <br /> As for Eden, that is easily ignored. The porters simply didn't encounter them / it blew up / or the porters found planet of slaves controlled by a few remaining twisted aberrants that needed to be put down (which they did). I simply didn't include Eden in my games and never needed a reason, and still don't. Just wasn't a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way#post441130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading that Aesculapian purge too, it was Doyen over-reaction 101. Then, nothing about it in the Alien Encounter series. I expect it would have been a filler adventure between the end of AE: Deception and the Coalition ark arriving, but we may never know what the original intent there was there.<br /> How would you have split them, out of curiousity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, there wasn't really a purge, but more of an internal collapse - at least, that's how it was heading. I always liked the idea of Zweidler attempting to turn his Order around but screwing it up - leading a notable portion of Docs to abandon the Order in all but name, moving over to work with other Orders, Aeon or most likely as independent operators. I imagined the Aesculapians becoming much smaller, organizationally speaking, and much more focussed in some ways - never quite reaching the heights of popularity at an organizational level that they enjoyed pre Huang-Marr. I doubt they'd get purged though - docs are useful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way#post441130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you think the Doyen were doing what they do? If the aberrants are all gone, why do the Doyen give a damn about some dimensionally locked terrestrial creatures?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aberrants are not gone. Nova's are. Aberrants and Novas are not the same thing. See above about how I resolve that.<br /> <br /> As for the Doyen, well, there's suggestion that the Doyen are split into two camps, and that works for me. You have the one group responsible for advocating the Prometheus Chambers as a way to create weapons against taint. The rest that feel humanity as a whole should be wiped out to solve the problem of taint. Quite literally humanity are pawns in a proxy war between these two groups (as are the Chromatics). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way#post441130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nippon just makes really advanced hard-tech that no-one else can produce and sifted their land-mass prior to rebuilding themselves into a giant arcology over sixty years ago? Ok. I can see how that doesn't come up unless you rub the characters faces in it, but you never had head-canon to sort that strangeness out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Never needed it, never spent time on it. Simples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way#post441130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chromies would have been just fine in their home setting i imagine, but what about the 'Deceivers'? The 'human-like' aliens who were like gods and attracted the Doyen? More space-mad (i like that term), but very pretty abbies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Human like compared to space frogs. I always took that as there were some Aberrants that still looked a little human. See imagery for the attack on Research Outpost Vesta - sure, alien looking but far more human looking than a Chromatic. Aeon pg 67. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way#post441130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have my hands on Deception, but i thought there was an encounter with tainted Furies at the end there. -shrug- Might be my own head-canon growing wild, time for some pruning... I guess another hand-waved space-mad abbie would be fine for that element too, that's basically what i remember happened anyway - unless Rushing Mountain from Asia Ascendant was involved somehow.<br /> -shrug-</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Furies are in there. It mentions Aberrant DNA. I take that as 2120+ space mad abbie DNA, not Nova.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way#post441130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that you might've still used 418/Venezuela, is that because you still use it as a temporal clairsentient barrier?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Process 418 felt like fan-service trying to pull the three RPG's together, instead of advancing what I liked about the Aeon setting (as written in the core RPG book). I'm not entirely sure what i'd do with it. I never advanced the timeline that far in my campaigns so it wasn't a thing. In any event, I would absolutely not have it unleashing non-prometheus chamber created powers into the setting. I'd likely have it mess with psionic powers for a time, but not make it a focus of any games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way#post441130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-standing ovation-<br /> Good riddance Apollo Milliken! I have a tough time with Apollo too - even in my world view, i would have done that a bit differently - but it does bring stuff together (Upeo purge &amp; the Chromie Fleet). I was kind of putting my eggs in the 'mind of a child' basket with him, an idiot wild-card who wants to be a comic book hero. Major Kid Miracleman/Superboy Prime vibes there. But just blowing him up would have made the next couple of years a bit less confronting for the Orders/Doyen. Your players never found the destruction of the Chromatic fleet warranted a less hand-wavey solution?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not once, nope. They assumed that a bunch of powerful teleporters actually got together to do it as there were no rules for porter powers at that point suggesting how tough that would be. They assumed that some porters were protecting the remote human colonies as best they could - as quietly as they could. That worked for me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way#post441130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really liked the teleporters as PCs, kind of like having a 2008 Nova in amongst the psion party with stronger versions of Warp, Teleport and teleport mastery (if memory serves). As non-Upeo PCs that would have sucked - everyone would've wanted to play Upeo/Starcrossed. But they <i>are</i> required for all but one extra-solar colonies (the bastards stopped all the generational arks, my poor, precious hard-science) and i wasn't letting go of that part of the setting for any reason - so the Upeo must remain. -sigh-<br /> Rebalancing the Teleportation modes may do a lot to address that, but teleporters prevent the setting from embracing light speed and relativistic travel, which is kind of sad - but baked in at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed - never advanced the timeline to the porters being back so it was easy to avoid dealing with them. That (aside from setting blending) is one thing I'm apprehensive about with the new edition. I'll probably need to write them out. We'll see.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:05:28-07:00","id":442916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my mind the Chibs abilities were a check against the Aberrants that survived the war and went out to the stars - not Novas (who in my view all joined Divis Mal in his pocket universe). In my view, aside from a couple major players like Divis Mal and some Novas who went with him, most Aberrants left at the end of the Aberrant war were already pretty much driven crazy by their taint. Its these guys that head off to the stars where they mutate even further - much closer to 2120 era Aberrants as presented in the Aeon core book. These are what the Doyen, Qin and Coalition encounter. They're barely recognizable as Nova's (a term that didn't start getting used until the Aberrant RPG was published, much later).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never been a fan of Mal's rumored universe egress - but that isn't relevant here. If i slip into 'Nova' occasionally, it's just an artefact of those 2120 tainted-nova games i ran, where the end game was always: you <i>will</i> go insane and become a monster - forgive my error of semantics. You have an issue with 2120 'Aberrants' and 2008 'Novas' being <i>narratively</i> (as opposed to rules-wise) the same though? I mean they specifically mention Soguk Birlesme on pg 71 of the core book.<br /> I don't really need the comic allusions of the Aberrant RPG, but 2120 space-mad aberrants up to that scale are really part of the fun for me. Those things are <i>terrifying</i> malignancies on reality and can even make the Doyen sympathetic.<br /> I don't think we really disagree there, but we might have to clarify our terms to be sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chibs were purged for a whole bunch of reasons, the one trotted out the most was 'in league with Aberrants'. As always with the Aeon setting, there's a bunch more going on. The Chibs experimenting far outside the boundaries the Doyen had hoped, S. K. Bhurano's refusal to back down when it all came to a head, personality conflicts between the Proxies, the Order's being terrified of humanity perceiving psions as just another type of Aberrant that should be collectively destroyed (a fear that comes up again later in the Huang-Marr incident). I'd put good money on Aeon screwing things up a couple times along the way too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it when there is more than meets the eye.<br /> This is actually decent reasoning - would you say the Doyen weren't really driving the purge, although they might have been part of the whole? Care to pitch an example of Aeon fumbling here?<br /> If you do ever get around to India Underground, let me know if that fits in - i won't speak for you, but i get the impression a lot of it would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, this wasn't a purge. There was an attempt to control, not wipe-out. It may be splitting hairs, but there's an important distinction. One of the big problems here is that Alex Cassel and Bolade Atwan really didn't get along. She point blank didn't trust the guy (probably with good reason, on reflection). Miscommunication, poor planning on behalf of the Proxies, a bit of not necessarily unwarranted paranoia from Atwan and yeah, power-keg ready to happen. They all fled because Atwan made it quite clear that remaining meant being stripped of your teleportation powers. Not much of a choice, really. Those left behind were not porters anymore, with the exception of some on the far colonies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, how would the Upeo have their powers stripped? Was there a permanent way of doing this? I seem to remember some biotech, but i don't remember it chemically 'un-dunking' the target psion... I would expect to remember that, but it wouldn't be my first experience with selective memory.<br /> Otherwise, this also makes sense. I never really trusted Cassel either. -smile- There is a bit of clash with the way the Upeo were presented in Stellar Frontier (remaining close to the colonies out of sheer humanity - but assuming the Esperanza attack was nothing but a hoax when they could have just looked for themselves), but i gather this was one of the official sources that you had issue with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Eden, that is easily ignored. The porters simply didn't encounter them / it blew up / or the porters found planet of slaves controlled by a few remaining twisted aberrants that needed to be put down (which they did). I simply didn't include Eden in my games and never needed a reason, and still don't. Just wasn't a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a pretty clean cut too for those wishing to stick to the 2120 core, i also kept my players (even the tainted campaign) as far away from Eden as possible. Still, i would be hungry for a bit more meat in there about the Upeo buggering off like they did - personal preference i guess. I'm not usually one for clear-cut good/evil, but i really wanted to blame someone for that.<br /> -shakes fist-<br /> Spoiler: I blamed the Doyen, those Order purging bastards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yeah, there wasn't really a purge, but more of an internal collapse - at least, that's how it was heading. I always liked the idea of Zweidler attempting to turn his Order around but screwing it up - leading a notable portion of Docs to abandon the Order in all but name, moving over to work with other Orders, Aeon or most likely as independent operators. I imagined the Aesculapians becoming much smaller, organizationally speaking, and much more focussed in some ways - never quite reaching the heights of popularity at an organizational level that they enjoyed pre Huang-Marr. I doubt they'd get purged though - docs are useful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, QKs and Teleporters were useful too, but i see where you are coming from and i actually like the idea of the Docs falling apart. It seems the administration and the membership are deeply at odds with each other from what we see in Passage through Shadow. I don't see many of the Orders lasting that long in the greater scale of things. I can't see the Aesculapians falling immediately however (Montressor! and the clinics give them a lot of good will), so the idea of Zweidler bollocksing up the rebuilding is appealing to me also.<br /> Good thinking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aberrants are not gone. Nova's are. Aberrants and Novas are not the same thing. See above about how I resolve that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Narratively, or system-wise? There is some evidence of the 'Aberrants' of 2008 and the space-mad monstrosities of 2120 are at least meant to be the same thing in a historical sense (Soguk Birlesme). Sure they are mutated and insane to the edge of obscenity by 2120, but in a narrative sense it was all the same thing, right?<br /> This isn't relevant to this point in particular, but i'm getting a bit mixed up on those semantics. Help me out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Doyen, well, there's suggestion that the Doyen are split into two camps, and that works for me. You have the one group responsible for advocating the Prometheus Chambers as a way to create weapons against taint. The rest that feel humanity as a whole should be wiped out to solve the problem of taint. Quite literally humanity are pawns in a proxy war between these two groups (as are the Chromatics).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're pretty much on the same page there, then. You are right, regardless of whether they are 2120 Taint-bastards or 2008 Quantum-bastards, the Doyen remain consistent. Excuse my brain-fart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Never needed it, never spent time on it. Simples.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm jealous, my players were raising eyebrows at the sequestration and sifting of Honshu right out of the core book. I had to avoid it like Eden for a while until Asia Ascendant came along. I'm hearing you, out of sight, out of mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human like compared to space frogs. I always took that as there were some Aberrants that still looked a little human. See imagery for the attack on Research Outpost Vesta - sure, alien looking but far more human looking than a Chromatic. Aeon pg 67.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> You have me dead to rights here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Furies are in there. It mentions Aberrant DNA. I take that as 2120+ space mad abbie DNA, not Nova.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, fair enough, i don't know why i thought that was even pertinent now...<br /> -muses-<br /> That's right, i thought there might have been some suggestion that the Breeder phyle has extracted the DNA for Quantum/Taint manipulation from the infamous first contact with humans. That might have suggested that Taint remains a genetic possibility within humanity into 2120. But nothing you have said here refutes that possibility, unless i'm not reading you right...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Process 418 felt like fan-service trying to pull the three RPG's together, instead of advancing what I liked about the Aeon setting (as written in the core RPG book). I'm not entirely sure what i'd do with it. I never advanced the timeline that far in my campaigns so it wasn't a thing. In any event, I would absolutely not have it unleashing non-prometheus chamber created powers into the setting. I'd likely have it mess with psionic powers for a time, but not make it a focus of any games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, i would not see the point of process 418 either if not for my personal (and monetary) comittment to the triple setting conundrum. I'm confortable with all three genres, but Sci-Fi is what brought me to the TU, not Super Heroes or Pulp Adventure.<br /> I've mentiioned this before, but i had never even seen the cover of Aberrant when i got it sent out via mail - i was honestly expecting... i don't know, but it wasn't comic super heroes, that's for sure. Adding them as mutated Lovecraftian space-horrors seemed to work (for a bit) though and the idea of bolstering the baseline via <i>some</i> of the rules presented in Adventure for paramorphs also appealed to me as a concept (plus, i was personally invested in the meta-plot by then).<br /> -shrug-<br /> I support you not having to use this. Even crossing over the three games, the setting doesn't really require another Hammersmith event, but i expected it to be <i>the</i> game-changer against the Coalition invasion down the line with the narrative lampshade hanging over it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not once, nope. They assumed that a bunch of powerful teleporters actually got together to do it as there were no rules for porter powers at that point suggesting how tough that would be. They assumed that some porters were protecting the remote human colonies as best they could - as quietly as they could. That worked for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so impressed by the adaptive inner logic of players sometimes, that actually makes sense if you don't have the teleporting rules to invalidate the idea. I'm guessing my physics-major player might have balked at the scales if i suggested that, but it certainly gets us over the line if the players accept it. Nice work there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442556#post442556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed - never advanced the timeline to the porters being back so it was easy to avoid dealing with them. That (aside from setting blending) is one thing I'm apprehensive about with the new edition. I'll probably need to write them out. We'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they intend to start after the porters are back then they will have a lot of work to recreate the intrigues of the original 2120 core. You lose the lost colonies, the Esperanza mystery, the Chromatic invasion (which leads to their return sequentially) and pick up a lot of bad press for the other orders in the process (assuming player sympathies go to the Upeo). I can't even really see the Colony forces surviving for long once the warfleets start teleporting about either, which leaves another hole.<br /> I can see where the demand might come from (teleporting is kewl), but there is a bit of narrative void to fill in there to get some of those iconic 2120 mysteries replaced too. Not sure how i feel about that, but if the team were able to come up with some crash-hot stuff in the appropriate vein to replace it, i guess i <i>could</i> go for that.... Maybe...?<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> A lot of what ifs and maybes here - all we can do is wait for now. It can be pretty frustrating when i get in the mood to write shit down for the setting, but i don't know what the setting is going to look like come the morrow.<br /> -looks at watch-<br /> <br /> So, just to finish up:<br /> How do you see the Coalition invasion going down?<br /> Can you give me/us an idea of which official 2120 supplements/material you simply could not fit into your vision and why?<br /> And just for a bit of romance, let's hear your favorite elements of the setting - the things that you would hate to let go of in the name of unity between the games - or point me to a post where you've spelled this out for the Onyx Path staff previously.<br /> Great post, CHILL. Very insightful and thought provoking. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Please forgive any lack of editing on my part.<br /> I may finally get my Darkness Revealed books out of storage one day and find some other tidbits, but you may consider yourself accounted for, for now.<br /> -bangs gavel-<br /> <br /> If anyone else is interested, feel free to take issue or lend support as you deem necessary, sorry for the initial exclusivity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T08:53:53-07:00","id":444322,"title":"","content":"I think, from the ongoing thread, I'm sensing that you have been in a position where you've needed to explain or otherwise expand on your reasoning for various concepts in the games you've run. It might be useful to understand that I haven't. Most of my player's have read only a handful of the books, and certainly don't collect everything for Aeon. We also have a longstanding understanding that if the GM responds to a question that that a certain option, or setting component isn't part of the game then we accept it and move on. No arguing over the historical references in various books or lamenting a lack of certain powers. It didn't happen, or it wasn't important or isn't available. Most of the time players tend to get what the GM is shooting for and roll with it, so its very rarely a problem. We're more interested in getting on with the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been a fan of Mal's rumored universe egress - but that isn't relevant here. If i slip into 'Nova' occasionally, it's just an artefact of those 2120 tainted-nova games i ran, where the end game was always: you <i>will</i> go insane and become a monster - forgive my error of semantics. You have an issue with 2120 'Aberrants' and 2008 'Novas' being <i>narratively</i> (as opposed to rules-wise) the same though? I mean they specifically mention Soguk Birlesme on pg 71 of the core book.<br /> I don't really need the comic allusions of the Aberrant RPG, but 2120 space-mad aberrants up to that scale are really part of the fun for me. Those things are <i>terrifying</i> malignancies on reality and can even make the Doyen sympathetic.<br /> I don't think we really disagree there, but we might have to clarify our terms to be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any reference to novas, named otherwise alluded to, is a note in history and simply not part of my Aeon setting games. I could go point by point, but that's not how I approach it. If there's any reference to something in 2120+ that is from the Nova era (Eden, specific Novas etc) then they simply aren't around anymore. The only thing left are twisted space-mad aberrants, and lots of them (and its these that met the Qin, Doyen, Coalition etc). The Colony is the biggest baddest of the bunch and is now so far removed from a Nova as to make the point irrelevant for me. I also never plan to use The Colony so I can easily handwave that. Novas and Aberrants are not, narratively or rules wise the same, in my games. The share a lineage, that's it. There are no Novas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it when there is more than meets the eye.<br /> This is actually decent reasoning - would you say the Doyen weren't really driving the purge, although they might have been part of the whole? Care to pitch an example of Aeon fumbling here?<br /> If you do ever get around to India Underground, let me know if that fits in - i won't speak for you, but i get the impression a lot of it would.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't spent any time thinking about it and don't feel a need to. The chib purge is part of the game's (granted recent) history, and not something I intend to cover in my games. I'm not that interested in potential chib powers being in my Aeon games either, so this was easy. They're gone, the Order's purged them as they admitted they were working with Aberrants. Absolutely players will assume there's more to that, but its not a focus of my games like 100+ other things mentioned in the books. So it doesn't really come up for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, how would the Upeo have their powers stripped? Was there a permanent way of doing this? I seem to remember some biotech, but i don't remember it chemically 'un-dunking' the target psion... I would expect to remember that, but it wouldn't be my first experience with selective memory.<br /> Otherwise, this also makes sense. I never really trusted Cassel either. -smile- There is a bit of clash with the way the Upeo were presented in Stellar Frontier (remaining close to the colonies out of sheer humanity - but assuming the Esperanza attack was nothing but a hoax when they could have just looked for themselves), but i gather this was one of the official sources that you had issue with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolade Atwan was doing it during when the porters left. Bolade had a 'you're with me or you're no longer porter' approach. There were members of the Upeo who stayed behind after having their powers stripped by the Proxy. Its mentioned in the fiction on page 53 of Stellar Frontiers (Atwan having done it four times already that day).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a pretty clean cut too for those wishing to stick to the 2120 core, i also kept my players (even the tainted campaign) as far away from Eden as possible. Still, i would be hungry for a bit more meat in there about the Upeo buggering off like they did - personal preference i guess. I'm not usually one for clear-cut good/evil, but i really wanted to blame someone for that.<br /> -shakes fist-<br /> Spoiler: I blamed the Doyen, those Order purging bastards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Stellar Frontier's is not my favorite book. Wasn't a fan of the porter powers being documented, Eden, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, QKs and Teleporters were useful too, but i see where you are coming from and i actually like the idea of the Docs falling apart. It seems the administration and the membership are deeply at odds with each other from what we see in Passage through Shadow. I don't see many of the Orders lasting that long in the greater scale of things. I can't see the Aesculapians falling immediately however (Montressor! and the clinics give them a lot of good will), so the idea of Zweidler bollocksing up the rebuilding is appealing to me also.<br /> Good thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure, QK's and Porters were useful, but a small army of selfless healers out on the streets offering direct, immediate 'magical' medical assistance to the public? That's a very easy sell, PR-wise. Zweidler will still, in my opinion, screw it up - he's not a strong leader and he has some very shady characters working for him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratively, or system-wise? There is some evidence of the 'Aberrants' of 2008 and the space-mad monstrosities of 2120 are at least meant to be the same thing in a historical sense (Soguk Birlesme). Sure they are mutated and insane to the edge of obscenity by 2120, but in a narrative sense it was all the same thing, right?<br /> This isn't relevant to this point in particular, but i'm getting a bit mixed up on those semantics. Help me out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both. See my points earlier.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm jealous, my players were raising eyebrows at the sequestration and sifting of Honshu right out of the core book. I had to avoid it like Eden for a while until Asia Ascendant came along. I'm hearing you, out of sight, out of mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really out of sight out of mind. More a mutual understanding that one GM's take on a setting is going to be different to another's and players accept that. -shrug-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, fair enough, i don't know why i thought that was even pertinent now...<br /> -muses-<br /> That's right, i thought there might have been some suggestion that the Breeder phyle has extracted the DNA for Quantum/Taint manipulation from the infamous first contact with humans. That might have suggested that Taint remains a genetic possibility within humanity into 2120. But nothing you have said here refutes that possibility, unless i'm not reading you right...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, again see at the top about 'any references to novas'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, i would not see the point of process 418 either if not for my personal (and monetary) comittment to the triple setting conundrum. I'm confortable with all three genres, but Sci-Fi is what brought me to the TU, not Super Heroes or Pulp Adventure.<br /> I've mentiioned this before, but i had never even seen the cover of Aberrant when i got it sent out via mail - i was honestly expecting... i don't know, but it wasn't comic super heroes, that's for sure. Adding them as mutated Lovecraftian space-horrors seemed to work (for a bit) though and the idea of bolstering the baseline via <i>some</i> of the rules presented in Adventure for paramorphs also appealed to me as a concept (plus, i was personally invested in the meta-plot by then).<br /> -shrug-<br /> I support you not having to use this. Even crossing over the three games, the setting doesn't really require another Hammersmith event, but i expected it to be <i>the</i> game-changer against the Coalition invasion down the line with the narrative lampshade hanging over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its really easy when you don't cross the game lines too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so impressed by the adaptive inner logic of players sometimes, that actually makes sense if you don't have the teleporting rules to invalidate the idea. I'm guessing my physics-major player might have balked at the scales if i suggested that, but it certainly gets us over the line if the players accept it. Nice work there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm.. if I had a physics major balking at anything I'd remind him/her that this was an epic sci-fi game with psionic powers, near-sentient biotechnology and faster than light travel. Leave physics at the door and enjoy the game already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they intend to start after the porters are back then they will have a lot of work to recreate the intrigues of the original 2120 core. You lose the lost colonies, the Esperanza mystery, the Chromatic invasion (which leads to their return sequentially) and pick up a lot of bad press for the other orders in the process (assuming player sympathies go to the Upeo). I can't even really see the Colony forces surviving for long once the warfleets start teleporting about either, which leaves another hole.<br /> I can see where the demand might come from (teleporting is kewl), but there is a bit of narrative void to fill in there to get some of those iconic 2120 mysteries replaced too. Not sure how i feel about that, but if the team were able to come up with some crash-hot stuff in the appropriate vein to replace it, i guess i <i>could</i> go for that.... Maybe...?<br /> -shrug-</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... you've listed all the major reasons I'm apprehensive about having the teleporters back (and available as PC's, as well). Guess we'll find out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of what ifs and maybes here - all we can do is wait for now. It can be pretty frustrating when i get in the mood to write shit down for the setting, but i don't know what the setting is going to look like come the morrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, indeed. It'll get here, will be an interesting read for sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-looks at watch-<br /> <br /> So, just to finish up:<br /> How do you see the Coalition invasion going down?<br /> Can you give me/us an idea of which official 2120 supplements/material you simply could not fit into your vision and why?<br /> And just for a bit of romance, let's hear your favorite elements of the setting - the things that you would hate to let go of in the name of unity between the games - or point me to a post where you've spelled this out for the Onyx Path staff previously.<br /> Great post, CHILL. Very insightful and thought provoking. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coalition: Not thought about it that much. I'd imagine the Doyen might split into two real, warring factions - with humanity having to side with one against the other or risk continuing to be relegated to pawn status. I suspect 'nice Doyen', porters, rest of the Orders and some newfound Chromatic friends plus the Qin might be enough to tackle the Arc.<br /> <br /> Supplements: Not so much complete supplements, but Stellar Frontiers, Terra Verde from the nova/process 418 perspective don't fit. It really depends on the specific content and context.<br /> <br /> What would I hate to let go in the name of unity: I'm not sold on the idea that setting unity is a good idea and something that should be sought in the first place. That question aside though - I'd hate to see Aeon (as in 2120+) lose its sense of shades of gray and its grittiness. I like the politicking, the intrigue, the shady deals, the dysfunctional nature of the Orders, that psions have it hard against possibly overwhelming foes with more raw power than they do. There was an offhand remark somewhere (RPG net?) about thinking of the Trinity Continuum as a 'World of Brightness'. That description suggests the opposite of what I'm interested in and what I feel makes Aeon an interesting setting. To be fair that comment was quickly pulled back a bit, but still....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=442916#post442916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great post, CHILL. Very insightful and thought provoking. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, I've enjoyed reading your posts mate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 03-16-2015, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:09:27-07:00","id":444567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, from the ongoing thread, I'm sensing that you have been in a position where you've needed to explain or otherwise expand on your reasoning for various concepts in the games you've run. It might be useful to understand that I haven't. Most of my player's have read only a handful of the books, and certainly don't collect everything for Aeon. We also have a longstanding understanding that if the GM responds to a question that that a certain option, or setting component isn't part of the game then we accept it and move on. No arguing over the historical references in various books or lamenting a lack of certain powers. It didn't happen, or it wasn't important or isn't available. Most of the time players tend to get what the GM is shooting for and roll with it, so its very rarely a problem. We're more interested in getting on with the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>-lots of nodding-<br /> I probably put myself in that position, i all but forced my players to read the coloured sections of the relevant books i had, so i didn't have to run preludes long into the night. Your approach to Aeon seems more like my approach to homebrew D&amp;D/pathfinder settings, where what i say goes, period. But in those days i was much more open to brief rules discussions, by the end of my 2120 tainted campaign, shit was getting so bogged down in rules and conflicting interpretations, i wasn't really enjoying the setting as much anymore. So in that way i prefer your approach. Like i've mentioned before, i did get a stealth 'nova' campaign that had heaps more promise, but it never got as far as i would have liked. The best approach for me was Darkness Revealed into Alien Encounter - despite generally preferring to improv rather than run out of a book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any reference to novas, named otherwise alluded to, is a note in history and simply not part of my Aeon setting games. I could go point by point, but that's not how I approach it. If there's any reference to something in 2120+ that is from the Nova era (Eden, specific Novas etc) then they simply aren't around anymore. The only thing left are twisted space-mad aberrants, and lots of them (and its these that met the Qin, Doyen, Coalition etc). The Colony is the biggest baddest of the bunch and is now so far removed from a Nova as to make the point irrelevant for me. I also never plan to use The Colony so I can easily handwave that. Novas and Aberrants are not, narratively or rules wise the same, in my games. The share a lineage, that's it. There are no Novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, taking the two things as seperate branches on a tree makes good sense (even for the unified settings), if i'm reading you right. The aberrants (novas) of their era are completely seperate from aberrants a century later, whether any of the original branch are still around isn't important anymore. So, for example; old Anders Nash turned/erupted/whatever back in whenever as a fully tainted aberrant - genetically/noetically (or whatever) divorced from whatever the Mals and Birlesmes of their era were. Do pull me up if i'm still not getting it.<br /> I brought up Dr. Birlesme because that's an aberrant era name that is recognized in the original source material, but i assume he went ass-mad just like the others. I also get the sense that i'm asking you to explain Babylon 5 from a Star Trek perspective (or vice versa, depending on preference) - there is a real mutual exclusivity, i can respect that. But for me to discard so many years of thought into it would be personally crushing. I can respectfully agree to disagree here if we must, but it's still excellent food for thought too.<br /> Anecdotally, i was way too close to having to write <i>the Colony</i> up as an actual NPC for the tainted campaign - but i stopped short of getting that far. How wrong is that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't spent any time thinking about it and don't feel a need to. The chib purge is part of the game's (granted recent) history, and not something I intend to cover in my games. I'm not that interested in potential chib powers being in my Aeon games either, so this was easy. They're gone, the Order's purged them as they admitted they were working with Aberrants. Absolutely players will assume there's more to that, but its not a focus of my games like 100+ other things mentioned in the books. So it does</div> </div> </div> </div>I 100% support the drive toward grey-scales and mysterious motives. I actually used the India Underground setting as prelude material for a paranoid Aesculapian who only escaped being caught up in the purge due to (mis)fortune, they ended up being one of the best 2120 PCs i've ever had the privilege to ST, but i never really got around to properly employing Quantakinesis as the book detailed. I did play with the idea, but never actually got there.<br /> -chuckles briefly at you being a credited author of the Chitra Bhanu web supplement-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bolade Atwan was doing it during when the porters left. Bolade had a 'you're with me or you're no longer porter' approach. There were members of the Upeo who stayed behind after having their powers stripped by the Proxy. Its mentioned in the fiction on page 53 of Stellar Frontiers (Atwan having done it four times already that day).<br /> <br /> Yeah, Stellar Frontier's is not my favorite book. Wasn't a fan of the porter powers being documented, Eden, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit, Proxies could do that? Good memory, there, thanks for pointing it out. I guess there could be some element of threat going on, but where there's smoke...<br /> I love space, it's one of the core elements that draws me to sci-fi, so Stellar Frontiers was a must buy for me and subsequently a must use due to my limited funds for gaming. But i've spent too much time behind the screen to let those particular powers get into the hands of my players.<br /> -shivers-<br /> Glad i wasn't alone on that point. The Upeo have a place in the setting, it's hardwired, but as PCs/rulesets they weren't quite right. Maybe there is a solution, but i haven't spent much time considering it. Those capable of becoming teleporters are quite clearly stated as being rare, helpfully.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh sure, QK's and Porters were useful, but a small army of selfless healers out on the streets offering direct, immediate 'magical' medical assistance to the public? That's a very easy sell, PR-wise. Zweidler will still, in my opinionm, screw it up - he's not a strong leader and he has some very shady characters working for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because i was leaning toward the Doyen being even worse that aberrants in my world view i might have gone as far as a purge. But i never got that far, so your version is just as applicable and much better for the Order's sustainability - it would all depend on where you wanted to take it after that point. Zweidler ruining his own order is deeply amusing to me however, i'd seriously consider using that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really out of sight out of mind. More a mutual understanding that one GM's take on a setting is going to be different to another's and players accept that. -shrug-</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm too curious for my own good sometimes, i hear a compelling idea and can be left wondering. I like to have a clear vision for improvisational purposes, so when the vision gets opaque in my mind i have to address it or avoid it. But that approach leads to a lot of wild head-canon too. You're right, good players are always willing to accept the ST/GM/DM/Keepers final call, but sufficiantly muddied waters leave <i>me</i> doubting that final call at times.<br /> Excuse me, i believe my insecurity may be showing.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its really easy when you don't cross the game lines too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The part of me that first bought Aeon/Trinity as a dark Sci-Fi setting will always be jealous of that simplicity, but as i demonstrated in that old handout i found, i was narratively headed for a collision even back then. I should have invested in battleground rather than aberrant, but i've never been a war-gamer and i'm not even sure it was out at that point.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm.. if I had a physics major balking at anything I'd remind him/her that this was an epic sci-fi game with psionic powers, near-sentient biotechnology and faster than light travel. Leave physics at the door and enjoy the game already.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was leaning more toward hard Sci-Fi, so i always took scientific advice onboard. But the ship had already kind of sailed on that in a way, i was just doing what i could to stay consistent. If my sci-fi game had no room for science, then i might as well have gone back to WOD or something. But i understand my approach on that front wasn't really what the game intended, hence my (still) ongoing attempt to define and explain the counter-intuitive technology and science of 2120.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coalition: Not thought about it that much. I'd imagine the Doyen might split into two real, warring factions - with humanity having to side with one against the other or risk continuing to be relegated to pawn status. I suspect 'nice Doyen', porters, rest of the Orders and some newfound Chromatic friends plus the Qin might be enough to tackle the Arc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. We have the same basic solution in mind (new and old allies coming together to save the earth), plus you get to avoid Apollo 'glory hog' Milliken in your version. -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supplements: Not so much complete supplements, but Stellar Frontiers, Terra Verde from the nova/process 418 perspective don't fit. It really depends on the specific content and context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but not too much relatively. I have a better sense of where you are coming from now. Did you have a favorite supplement, just to counterbalance this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would I hate to let go in the name of unity: I'm not sold on the idea that setting unity is a good idea and something that should be sought in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd hate for you to be left out in the cold, because i think your vision has a lot to offer, even for the unification side of things. But we may have to agree to disagree on that point a bit, because i've invested too much of my own time trying to sort that mess out. Of course, i'm happy to keep doing so in my own lonely corner - just as a thought excercise. I may occasionally reach out to get your perspective on things, because i don't think anything really needs to be too dramatically changed for unity, just some details here and there and <i>maybe</i> a few hard-wired concepts could be phrased a little differently. You seem to have a very solid grasp of the basics and i'm not (consciously) in the game of changing that, because it's what got me so interested in the first place.<br /> Do pull me up if i'm ever stepping on those 2120 toes...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That question aside though - I'd hate to see Aeon (as in 2120+) lose its sense of shades of gray and its grittiness. I like the politicking, the intrigue, the shady deals, the dysfunctional nature of the Orders, that psions have it hard against possibly overwhelming foes with more raw power than they do. There was an offhand remark somewhere (RPG net?) about thinking of the Trinity Continuum as a 'World of Brightness'. That description suggests the opposite of what I'm interested in and what I feel makes Aeon an interesting setting. To be fair that comment was quickly pulled back a bit, but still....</div> </div> </div> </div>You are preaching to the choir. -smile-<br /> 'World of Brightness' is mentioned in the 'what we know' document, immediately giving me douche chills. That isn't what i'm up for, glad to see i'm not alone. If i could find someone with that perspective i'd call them to account too.<br /> -scans the horizon predatorially-<br /> Glad to hear there was some back-pedalling involved there-after. i don't mind the Aeon society being some kind of binding glue, but singularly good (or evil) anything isn't a story concept i want to spend much time with - both perspectives should have their own merits for more interesting role-play opportunities.<br /> -goes searching for back-pedalling on 'world of brightness'-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444322#post444322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No problem, I've enjoyed reading your posts mate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The feeling is mutual, there's some good stuff in here and you've been a charming and challenging companion.<br /> i hope someone of pertinence is taking the time to consider your position on these specifics.<br /> -repeats last line, but louder for official ears-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Like i wasn't going to edit my post, shows how little you know. 03-16-2015, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:18:51-07:00","id":444971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your approach to Aeon seems more like my approach to homebrew D&amp;D/pathfinder settings, where what i say goes, period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhat.....perhaps. Its more that I never really have to play hardball about it. Very experienced and flexible players not overly interested in crunchy stuff helps a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, taking the two things as seperate branches on a tree makes good sense (even for the unified settings), if i'm reading you right. The aberrants (novas) of their era are completely seperate from aberrants a century later, whether any of the original branch are still around isn't important anymore. So, for example; old Anders Nash turned/erupted/whatever back in whenever as a fully tainted aberrant - genetically/noetically (or whatever) divorced from whatever the Mals and Birlesmes of their era were. Do pull me up if i'm still not getting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, thats basically it. I could just as easily spin it that most novas that didn't vanish with Mal into 'wherever' evolved into twisted space made abbies quite early after the end of the Aberrant war, and its their descendants that came into contact with the Doyen etc. Either works for me. Funnily, it was never a question that came up for me........until the Aberrant RPG was published.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I brought up Dr. Birlesme because that's an aberrant era name that is recognized in the original source material, but i assume he went ass-mad just like the others. I also get the sense that i'm asking you to explain Babylon 5 from a Star Trek perspective (or vice versa, depending on preference) - there is a real mutual exclusivity, i can respect that. But for me to discard so many years of thought into it would be personally crushing. I can respectfully agree to disagree here if we must, but it's still excellent food for thought too.</div> </div> </div> </div>See above. Also, this is just my take, which works for me an my players. I wouldn't expect anyone else to take the slightest bit of notice of what I do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anecdotally, i was way too close to having to write <i>the Colony</i> up as an actual NPC for the tainted campaign - but i stopped short of getting that far. How wrong is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>O_o<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I 100% support the drive toward grey-scales and mysterious motives. I actually used the India Underground setting as prelude material for a paranoid Aesculapian who only escaped being caught up in the purge due to (mis)fortune, they ended up being one of the best 2120 PCs i've ever had the privilege to ST, but i never really got around to properly employing Quantakinesis as the book detailed. I did play with the idea, but never actually got there.<br /> -chuckles briefly at you being a credited author of the Chitra Bhanu web supplement-</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember.... 'facilitator' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit, Proxies could do that? Good memory, there, thanks for pointing it out. I guess there could be some element of threat going on, but where there's smoke...<br /> I love space, it's one of the core elements that draws me to sci-fi, so Stellar Frontiers was a must buy for me and subsequently a must use due to my limited funds for gaming. But i've spent too much time behind the screen to let those particular powers get into the hands of my players.<br /> -shivers-</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly caught my eye when I read it. Makes sense, actually, that they could do that. Another fail-safe for the Doyen perhaps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad i wasn't alone on that point. The Upeo have a place in the setting, it's hardwired, but as PCs/rulesets they weren't quite right. Maybe there is a solution, but i haven't spent much time considering it. Those capable of becoming teleporters are quite clearly stated as being rare, helpfully.</div> </div> </div> </div>There may well be, and perhaps its tackled this time in the new version. I think the concept of the Order is quite interesting, but the idea of teleporation as written was a bit much for me. Just a personal preference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because i was leaning toward the Doyen being even worse that aberrants in my world view i might have gone as far as a purge. But i never got that far, so your version is just as applicable and much better for the Order's sustainability - it would all depend on where you wanted to take it after that point. Zweidler ruining his own order is deeply amusing to me however, i'd seriously consider using that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's so many examples of organizational failure for the Aesculapians throughout the canon books (especially the DR books) that I really can't see how Zweidler gets it all back on track, not without sacrificing some of his control and moving the order away from the influence of his personality. But there's the problem, the Orders really do reflect the personality of their Proxy in many ways so.....yeah. Docs are probably screwed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm too curious for my own good sometimes, i hear a compelling idea and can be left wondering. I like to have a clear vision for improvisational purposes, so when the vision gets opaque in my mind i have to address it or avoid it. But that approach leads to a lot of wild head-canon too. You're right, good players are always willing to accept the ST/GM/DM/Keepers final call, but sufficiantly muddied waters leave <i>me</i> doubting that final call at times.<br /> Excuse me, i believe my insecurity may be showing.<br /> -smile-<br /> using that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I'm very fortunate where my players are concerned, and as a GM I'm not going to spend a lot of time rationalizing things. If I don't want it in there, its gone. Figure it out later (if at all, and only then if it comes up).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part of me that first bought Aeon/Trinity as a dark Sci-Fi setting will always be jealous of that simplicity, but as i demonstrated in that old handout i found, i was narratively headed for a collision even back then. I should have invested in battleground rather than aberrant, but i've never been a war-gamer and i'm not even sure it was out at that point.<br /> -shrug-</div> </div> </div> </div>Battleground doesn't do a lot for the RPG, but there's some interesting content in there. The Battleground Players Guide is available free on Drivethrurpg, I think. Its been years since I read it, and although there's probably a bunch of duplication with the RPG it may be worth digging through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was leaning more toward hard Sci-Fi, so i always took scientific advice onboard. But the ship had already kind of sailed on that in a way, i was just doing what i could to stay consistent. If my sci-fi game had no room for science, then i might as well have gone back to WOD or something. But i understand my approach on that front wasn't really what the game intended, hence my (still) ongoing attempt to define and explain the counter-intuitive technology and science of 2120.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough - I come at Aeon with an emphasis on the fiction, and much less on the science.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. We have the same basic solution in mind (new and old allies coming together to save the earth), plus you get to avoid Apollo 'glory hog' Milliken in your version. -smile-</div> </div> </div> </div>He blew up, remember :-P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but not too much relatively. I have a better sense of where you are coming from now. Did you have a favorite supplement, just to counterbalance this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Not so much a single supplement really. I love the core book, really enjoy America Offline - and, with all their faults, the DR series worked really well for me. Eh... I suspect you're interested in a 'if I had to name it' answer. The core book, then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd hate for you to be left out in the cold, because i think your vision has a lot to offer, even for the unification side of things. But we may have to agree to disagree on that point a bit, because i've invested too much of my own time trying to sort that mess out. Of course, i'm happy to keep doing so in my own lonely corner - just as a thought excercise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm absolutely, perfectly happy doing my own thing. If the new edition is so heavily intertwined that I need to start spending a bunch of time just to pull it apart, I'll not bother with it past the first book or two. I doubt that's going to be the case though. OPP have already suggested that each setting needs to be able to stand on its own, they've got the right team for it and definitely the right stewardship for it in Ian W as the uberdev. I'm fairly confident we'll get something that allows me to largely ignore the other settings other than Aeon.<br /> <br /> I probably haven't mentioned this, but I've also run Aberrant (the RPG, set in the early 2000's) and played it several times. As a GM it really didn't do it for me, and as a player it was OK - some good gming helped. The rules were a bit 'bucket of dice' for my tastes and PC's had some insane capabilities even when low powered, so it really wouldn't be my first choice of game to play. I'm not a bit fan of 'supers' anyway, so it just wasn't my thing. Its passable though, if you like that kinda stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may occasionally reach out to get your perspective on things, because i don't think anything really needs to be too dramatically changed for unity, just some details here and there and <i>maybe</i> a few hard-wired concepts could be phrased a little differently. You seem to have a very solid grasp of the basics and i'm not (consciously) in the game of changing that, because it's what got me so interested in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem - but remember, I have no information about the new version at all - I'm just a fan. I'm just the guy who setup EON and (apparently) had some fanfic writing credits. If anything, treat everything I say with an even bigger pinch of salt than you would for others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do pull me up if i'm ever stepping on those 2120 toes...</div> </div> </div> </div>Pffft...why would I? What you do with your games / version of Aeon is entirely up to you, mate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are preaching to the choir. -smile-<br /> 'World of Brightness' is mentioned in the 'what we know' document, immediately giving me douche chills. That isn't what i'm up for, glad to see i'm not alone. If i could find someone with that perspective i'd call them to account too.<br /> -scans the horizon predatorially-<br /> Glad to hear there was some back-pedalling involved there-after. i don't mind the Aeon society being some kind of binding glue, but singularly good (or evil) anything isn't a story concept i want to spend much time with - both perspectives should have their own merits for more interesting role-play opportunities.<br /> -goes searching for back-pedalling on 'world of brightness'-</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't think that phrase was a clear a description of intent with the new version as it initially seemed. Its buried away in this thread somewheres: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?738088-Aeon-The-%C6on-Trinity-which-branch-do-you-love-Which-branch-do-you-hate\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...ch-do-you-hate</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The feeling is mutual, there's some good stuff in here and you've been a charming and challenging companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome, same for you too - been fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444567#post444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i hope someone of pertinence is taking the time to consider your position on these specifics.<br /> -repeats last line, but louder for official ears-</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know. They don't. I'm good with that too. OPP needs to do what's best for the line, and that may mean my approach is less viable. I'm cool with that. I have enough stuff to work with as it is...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 03-16-2015, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T20:14:20-07:00","id":445268,"title":"","content":"(!) That was quick...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhat.....perhaps. Its more that I never really have to play hardball about it. Very experienced and flexible players not overly interested in crunchy stuff helps a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, between your A-Z anecdotes and other material, sounds like your players were a good group. My players are a pretty good bunch too, but i like to be challenged as well, so i encourage a little lip at times. But after my brother started running aberrant with access to all my books and another science major (chemistry this time) player picked up the core, there were a lot of questions that came up. As you can probably tell, i enjoyed fielding them. Although, many of my answers were merely smug permutations of 'you'll have to wait and see'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, thats basically it. I could just as easily spin it that most novas that didn't vanish with Mal into 'wherever' evolved into twisted space made abbies quite early after the end of the Aberrant war, and its their descendants that came into contact with the Doyen etc. Either works for me. Funnily, it was never a question that came up for me........until the Aberrant RPG was published.<br /> <br /> See above. Also, this is just my take, which works for me an my players. I wouldn't expect anyone else to take the slightest bit of notice of what I do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think i figured out where my fixation came from, the core book recommends 'Akira' as reference for aberrants. I had spent some time collecting that story and had just finished reading through the comics by that stage, Tetsuo Shima was imminently sympathetic and i transferred that pathos directly into the Trinity game. In the comics, the most evil characters were the corrupt government officials that kept forcing him into a corner and getting him hooked on the drugs while they bled neo-tokyo for everything they could. So by that reference - Aberrants by nature =/= Evil. Stupid, impulsive, crazy and weak maybe, but not fundamentally evil. There is even some shreds here and there that fed right into this (i beleive herzog saw taint as a disease?).<br /> <br /> I somewhat disagree, i think you have some valuable insight into what made the 2120s so compelling at the outset that some of us might have forgotten along the way. I look forward to reading your input going forward.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">O_o</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't have put it better myself!<br /> I kind of wonder if anyone actually did that without realizing what it would inevitably lead to...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember.... 'facilitator' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Author is funnier, but ok, <i>facilitator</i>.<br /> -smile-<br /> Like i'm the Trinity junkie and you're the local pusher.<br /> -nods sadly-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That certainly caught my eye when I read it. Makes sense, actually, that they could do that. Another fail-safe for the Doyen perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the more (potential) Doyen interferrence i see, the more entrenched my distrust of them. I wonder if this shows up in the other books, i seem to remember a clairsentient killer/criminal who would have been a prime candidate, but a quick skim through Luna Rising produced nothing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There may well be, and perhaps its tackled this time in the new version. I think the concept of the Order is quite interesting, but the idea of teleporation as written was a bit much for me. Just a personal preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the concept of having teleporters available right off the bat is going to need some good thinking to go with. I'm interested to see what OPP have planned for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's so many examples of organizational failure for the Aesculapians throughout the canon books (especially the DR books) that I really can't see how Zweidler gets it all back on track, not without sacrificing some of his control and moving the order away from the influence of his personality. But there's the problem, the Orders really do reflect the personality of their Proxy in many ways so.....yeah. Docs are probably screwed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throwing in the management-are-idiots trope could make this into a fun degeneration too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm very fortunate where my players are concerned, and as a GM I'm not going to spend a lot of time rationalizing things. If I don't want it in there, its gone. Figure it out later (if at all, and only then if it comes up).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, flow takes priority, but that 'vision' can be pretty important for my style. Apart from a few fun dialogues here and there, this stuff mostly came up out of game. My group were always willing to let me make the calls, i just wanted to be sure i had a payoff in mind that wouldn't break the setting or fall flat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Battleground doesn't do a lot for the RPG, but there's some interesting content in there. The Battleground Players Guide (is, I think available free on Drivethrurpg. Its been years since I read it, and although there's probably a bunch of duplication with the RPG it may be worth digging through.</div> </div> </div> </div>It very much is. A wealth of information about KLG, good information on high-level anti-aberrant responses and even a few tidbits that i don't remember ever seeing in the RPG books. Plus, the scant information about Kali and Yog-Death made the inner workings of the Colony forces much easier to tease out. I rarely ever broke it out as a wargame, but i never regretted purchasing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough - I come at Aeon with an emphasis on the fiction, and much less on the science.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fear that hardwired, bad-science could be a sore point for me, but i'm willing to write my own science material if the fiction material is strong enough and the (now dated) core still has a lot right in that regard. I think i'm one of the few who would cringe to think of Trinity as Psi-Fi - despite all the evidence that it already is.<br /> -hangs head-<br /> Story/fiction elements are still more important for gaming, but bad science can mess with immersion for me personally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Not so much a single supplement really. I love the core book, really enjoy America Offline - and, with all their faults, the DR series worked really well for me. Eh... I suspect you're interested in a 'if I had to name it' answer. The core book, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't need a single book in particular, this works. That 2120 core was <i>really</i> something special though, wasn't it? Great mysteries, decent futurism/sci-fi, bizarre aliens and enough intrigue to sink a boat once you started reading between the lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm absolutely, perfectly happy doing my own thing. If the new edition is so heavily intertwined that I need to start spending a bunch of time just to pull it apart, I'll not bother with it past the first book or two. I doubt that's going to be the case though. OPP have already suggested that each setting needs to be able to stand on its own, they've got the right team for it and definitely the right stewardship for it in Ian W as the uberdev. I'm fairly confident we'll get something that allows me to largely ignore the other settings other than Aeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it could be very good stuff. Unless it isn't...<br /> -smile-<br /> I loved the work on the STH, so i'm cautiously optimistic so far. I'll probably use the whole meta-plot, but my main concern is the 2120 stuff, if i want to use that, i'm sold. The only thing that has rubbed me the wrong way so far was the 'world of brightness' thing, but from what i gather it wasn't meant in the way i read it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably haven't mentioned this, but I've also run Aberrant (the RPG, set in the early 2000's) and played it several times. As a GM it really didn't do it for me, and as a player it was OK - some good gming helped. The rules were a bit 'bucket of dice' for my tastes and PC's had some insane capabilities even when low powered, so it really wouldn't be my first choice of game to play. I'm not a bit fan of 'supers' anyway, so it just wasn't my thing. Its passable though, if you like that kinda stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven't mentioned running Aberrant to me, that gives you more experience with that setting than i. I loved my comics growing up, but it was never my preferred RPG setting. My brother has run some great games out the Aberrant setting in a comic-book style, and we've both tried out some half-joking pulp throwbacks as lip service to Adventure or just a change of pace. But all my games in TU have been from the 2120s, which leaves me a little under-qualified on the other settings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No problem - but remember, I have no information about the new version at all - I'm just a fan. I'm just the guy who setup EON and (apparently) had some fanfic writing credits. If anything, treat everything I say with an even bigger pinch of salt than you would for others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no illusions, but i do think you see 2120 with a clarity some of us <i>might</i> not. I know you've reminded me personally of a few things that i've lost sight of along the way (the upeo purge wasn't necessarily as cut and dried, 2120 was still excellent even <i>without</i> the rest of the meta-plot, the plainly obvious difference between Novas and Aberrants, etc..) and we're all just fans waiting on official announcements from on high. I certainly don't trust you further than i could throw you, especially not to read anything.<br /> -tease-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pffft...why would I? What you do with your games / version of Aeon is entirely up to you, mate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean i would necessarily change my opinion because of you, silly CHILL, but it's good nostalgia and reminds me why i went balls deep in the first place.<br /> -smile-<br /> I'll probably use 418 as another Hammersmith just to piss off the Doyen, i'm not letting go of the Nihonjin Remnants because they assist in making the science interesting and i still think taint-doomed Novas have a place in 2120 along with paramorphs. But your approach is no less valid, the setting's versatility is one of its strongest assets - that goes for all three games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't think that phrase was a clear a description of intent with the new version as it initially seemed. Its buried away in this thread somewheres: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?738088-Aeon-The-%C6on-Trinity-which-branch-do-you-love-Which-branch-do-you-hate\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...ch-do-you-hate</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, thanks for that, my search-fu failed me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way?p=444971#post444971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, you know. They don't. I'm good with that too. OPP needs to do what's best for the line, and that may mean my approach is less viable. I'm cool with that. I have enough stuff to work with as it is...</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, whatever they have to do to keep the line running will be fine, i'm sure we'll all get a bone or three along the way at the least. I just really had fun with 2120 Trinity, so i consider your perspective noteworthy, or at least worthy of inspection. If the 2120s must move away from the grey scales, or toward bad science or whatever - i'll just be glad it's still around. It was entirely gone for a while there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Actually just fixing a typo this time, much less OCD than usual... 03-16-2015, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}